# Access control on value files: missing files answer 0xF0, a standard data
# file rejects value commands with 0x9D because they do not apply to that kind
# of object at all, and a file whose access rights require key 0 answers 0xAE
# until the session is authenticated with it.
#
# Generated from tests/test_dfc_virtual_picc_value_vectors.c (/access) by
# recording the exchanges the reference engine performed, then
# cross-checked: all 23 byte expectations asserted by that test matched
# the recording exactly.
#
# Re-recorded when access-rights refusals were split from wrong-object
# refusals. Only the two file 0x0B steps moved, from 0x9D to 0x9D's
# authentication counterpart 0xAE; the other 23 recorded steps were
# byte-identical to the previous recording.
#
# The two extra steps are the D40 authentication handshake, which the source
# performs via a helper and asserts only by status. RndB is pinned so the
# vector does not inherit the engine default generator.

